# Hyper-V opens an enhanced session over a Hyper-V socket to port 3389
# (VMConnect, and Hyper-V's own check of whether one is available), which
# arrives as a VMBus device whose class is that port's service ID. It does
# that only when the VM is set to the Hyper-V socket transport, which Linux
# needs, so patrone-hyperv-setup-seen.service notes it for Patrone Hyper-V
# Setup.
SUBSYSTEM=="vmbus", ACTION=="add", ATTR{class_id}=="{00000d3d-facb-11e6-bd58-64006a7986d3}", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="patrone-hyperv-setup-seen.service"
